# Both MTK power interface families are served from hal_power_default, on the
# device-private hal_mtk_power attribute rather than AOSP's hal_power_hwservice
# -- see power/hwservice.te. lshal on the handset shows exactly these four
# instances: mtkpower@1.0::IMtkPerf/default, mtkpower@1.0::IMtkPower/default,
# power@2.0::IPower/default and power@2.1::IPower/default, all with an empty
# client column. AOSP's android.hardware.power@1.0-1.3::IPower is registered by
# the same process and keeps its platform label.
# vendor.mediatek.hardware.power::IPerf is never registered and was removed.
vendor.mediatek.hardware.mtkpower::IMtkPerf   u:object_r:mtk_hal_power_hwservice:s0
vendor.mediatek.hardware.mtkpower::IMtkPower  u:object_r:mtk_hal_power_hwservice:s0
vendor.mediatek.hardware.power::IPower        u:object_r:mtk_hal_power_hwservice:s0

vendor.mediatek.hardware.netdagent::INetdagent u:object_r:mtk_netdagent_hwservice:s0
